  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as a universal moral observer",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any specific visual or scene element via deictic pronouns. However, the meme's overall intent and the textual material 'there is always good and bad in this world' implicitly project the user onto a position of moral judgment or philosophical contemplation. The user is invited to accept or reflect upon the simplistic moral dichotomy presented, thereby internalizing the meme's framing as a universal truth. This projection occurs through the textual material, which acts as a conceptual anchor for the user's interpretation of the visual juxtaposition.",
